# <type>(<scope>): <subject>          <- 72 chars max, imperative, no full stop
#
# Why this change, and what it costs. Wrap at 72. Leave it out only when the
# subject already says everything.
#
# Refs: ADR-00NN                      <- when the change follows or adds a decision
#
# type:   feat     a capability the user can see
#         fix      a defect, with the behaviour it restores
#         perf     same behaviour, measurably faster
#         refactor same behaviour, different shape
#         docs     documentation only, including ADRs and the guides
#         test     tests only
#         build    Cargo, pnpm, bundling, icons
#         ci       workflows
#         chore    anything with no effect on the shipped app
#
# scope:  core cli app ui calc storage market fx inflation import ai
#         dashboard i18n docs deps  (omit when the change is repo-wide)
#
# A breaking change adds ! after the scope and a "BREAKING CHANGE:" paragraph
# explaining what a user or a caller must now do differently.
